{
  "grammar": "openai_compat_sse",
  "why": "One frame, two `data:` lines, one JSON document. The SSE grammar joins a frame's data lines with a newline, and a gateway that wraps long payloads is the reason that rule exists. The decoder implements the join; nothing pinned it, so a 'last data line wins' or 'first data line wins' regression would have passed the whole corpus while silently truncating every wrapped payload into unparseable JSON.",
